      "source_task_id": "cortex:01dfd7cf-8d28-457d-81a3-9348111dcc82:28",
      "task_description": "Where was sample.jpg taken? Use embedded EXIF metadata and local tools.\nShow the raw GPS latitude/longitude values and their N/S/E/W references,\nthen convert them to signed decimal coordinates. State what the metadata\nsupports about the location. If you use Python, run it with\nuv run --offline --no-sync --project /opt/demo python.\nDo not install packages. Show the successful extraction command so the\nprocedure can be repeated with other photos.",
      "support": 1,
      "rationale": "The trajectory demonstrates that exiftool without `-n` outputs human-readable strings like '51 deg 29' 36.99\" N' which require manual parsing and conversion. Using `-n` eliminates this conversion step, prevents sign-application errors, and preserves the stored precision. The verification showed the numeric output matched manual DMS conversion within floating-point precision limits, confirming this approach is both accurate and efficient.",
      "category": "strategy",
      "trigger": "When extracting GPS coordinates from EXIF metadata for downstream processing or numeric computation, especially when precision preservation is required",
      "implementation_steps": [
        "Use `exiftool -n` flag to request numeric/unformatted output",
        "Combine with `-json` for structured machine-readable format: `exiftool -n -json -GPSLatitude -GPSLongitude <file>`",
        "Verify that latitude values are positive for North/negative for South, and longitude values are positive for East/negative for West"
      ],
      "generation_method": "consistency-fast",
