      "task_description": "Where was sample.jpg taken? Use embedded EXIF metadata and local tools.\nShow the raw GPS latitude/longitude values and their N/S/E/W references,\nthen convert them to signed decimal coordinates. State what the metadata\nsupports about the location. If you use Python, run it with\nuv run --offline --no-sync --project /opt/demo python.\nDo not install packages. Show the successful extraction command so the\nprocedure can be repeated with other photos.",
      "support": 1,
      "rationale": "The trajectory performed comprehensive verification by checking: (1) the numeric difference between manual DMS conversion and tool output (confirming precision), and (2) that signs matched reference tags (confirming correct hemisphere application). This caught potential errors where magnitude might be correct but sign wrong, or vice versa. The verification confirmed West=negative longitude and North=positive latitude were correctly applied.",
      "category": "strategy",
      "trigger": "When converting or extracting GPS coordinates from metadata formats that store hemisphere references separately from numeric values",
      "implementation_steps": [
        "Calculate or extract the decimal coordinate values",
        "Separately verify the sign matches the cardinal direction reference: North→positive latitude, South→negative latitude, East→positive longitude, West→negative longitude",
        "Check numeric precision by comparing against known reference values or manual conversion",
        "Report both magnitude accuracy and sign correctness in verification output"
      ],
